</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.5.2 </span>Training Reward</h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure a high weight on correctness relative to other components, we assign a
<span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">correctness reward</span> of <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+4</annotation></semantics></math> if the final answer is correct and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.
The <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">format reward</span> ranges from <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>: a score of <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> is given for the
presence of the <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;think&gt;</span> and <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/think&gt;</span> tokens, and an additional <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math>
is awarded if every reasoning trajectory is properly enclosed within these tokens in
the correct order. The <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">length reward</span> ranges from <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. The overall reward
is computed as the sum of these components:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Total Reward}=\text{Correctness Reward}+\text{Format Reward}+\text{Length Reward}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Total Reward</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Correctness Reward</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>Format Reward</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>Length Reward</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Total Reward}=\text{Correctness Reward}+\text{Format Reward}+\text{Length Reward}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.5.3 </span>Evaluation Metrics</h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each of the dataset we compute the accuracy and the average response length. Specifically for OverthinkingBench we also compute the <math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{AUC}_{\text{OAA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>AUC</mtext><mtext>OAA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{AUC}_{\text{OAA}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This metric is based on Overthinking-Adjusted Accuracy (OAA), which measures model correctness under a limit on reasoning tokens.
For a threshold <math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, it is defined as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{OAA}_{t}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\big(\text{Correctness}_{i}\cdot\mathbb{I}(\text{ThinkTokens}_{i}&lt;t)\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>OAA</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Correctness</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>ThinkTokens</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{OAA}_{t}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\big(\text{Correctness}_{i}\cdot\mathbb{I}(\text{ThinkTokens}_{i}&lt;t)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Correctness}_{i}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>Correctness</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Correctness}_{i}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates whether the <math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th response is correct, and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator function that enforces the thinking length constraint.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{AUC}_{\text{OAA}}=\int_{0}^{t_{\max}}\frac{\text{OAA}_{t}}{t_{\max}}\,dt\approx\frac{1}{t_{\max}}\sum_{t=0}^{t_{\max}}\text{OAA}_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>AUC</mtext><mtext>OAA</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><msub><mtext>OAA</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></munderover><msub><mtext>OAA</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{AUC}_{\text{OAA}}=\int_{0}^{t_{\max}}\frac{\text{OAA}_{t}}{t_{\max}}\,dt\approx\frac{1}{t_{\max}}\sum_{t=0}^{t_{\max}}\text{OAA}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum number of allowed thinking tokens. Furthermore, following the method from  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aggarwal et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, to compute the OptimalThinkingBench metric: F1 score we combine the <math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{AUC}_{\text{OAA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>AUC</mtext><mtext>OAA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{AUC}_{\text{OAA}}</annotation></semantics></math> from OverthinkingBench and Accuracy (<math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Acc}_{\mathrm{ut}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Acc</mi><mi>ut</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Acc}_{\mathrm{ut}}</annotation></semantics></math>) from UnderthinkingBench into a single F1 score:</p>
<table id="A1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F1=2\cdot\frac{\mathrm{AUC}_{\mathrm{OAA}}\cdot\mathrm{Acc}_{\mathrm{ut}}}{\mathrm{AUC}_{\mathrm{OAA}}+\mathrm{Acc}_{\mathrm{ut}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>AUC</mi><mi>OAA</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>Acc</mi><mi>ut</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>AUC</mi><mi>OAA</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Acc</mi><mi>ut</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F1=2\cdot\frac{\mathrm{AUC}_{\mathrm{OAA}}\cdot\mathrm{Acc}_{\mathrm{ut}}}{\mathrm{AUC}_{\mathrm{OAA}}+\mathrm{Acc}_{\mathrm{ut}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We computed <span id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">AUC</span><span id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">OAA</span> and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F{1}</annotation></semantics></math> scores using our own implementation, since the evaluation scripts from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheng et al. (2025)</a></cite> were not open-sourced.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.5.4 </span>Training prompt</h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each questions in the training set, instruction was provided: <span id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">‘‘Let’s think step by step and output the final answer within <math id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\backslash\backslash\text{{boxed}}\{\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>\</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">boxed</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\backslash\backslash\text{{boxed}}\{\}</annotation></semantics></math>’’</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Confidence based compression</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to attention compression, where a score is calculated for each reasoning token, the confidence of the model is used to calculate the score, and based on the lowest average score, reasoning steps are removed. <a href="#algorithm2" title="In A.6 Confidence based compression ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Think Right:​ Learning to Mitigate Under-Over Thinking via Adaptive, Attentive Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows the pseudocode used to calculate the confidence of each token.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span>Token Confidence Calculation</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm2.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Top-<math id="algorithm2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> token log-probabilities <math id="algorithm2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=\{\ell_{1},\ell_{2},\dots,\ell_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=\{\ell_{1},\ell_{2},\dots,\ell_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Confidence score <math id="algorithm2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">begin</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Convert log-probabilities to probabilities </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}\leftarrow\exp(\ell_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}\leftarrow\exp(\ell_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="algorithm2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{j}\in L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{j}\in L</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Normalize probabilities </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\leftarrow\sum_{j=1}^{k}p_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\leftarrow\sum_{j=1}^{k}p_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}\leftarrow p_{j}/Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}\leftarrow p_{j}/Z</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="algorithm2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Compute entropy of distribution </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H\leftarrow-\sum_{j=1}^{k}p_{j}\cdot\log(p_{j}+\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\leftarrow-\sum_{j=1}^{k}p_{j}\cdot\log(p_{j}+\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Maximum entropy with <math id="algorithm2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> tokens </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\max}\leftarrow\log(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\max}\leftarrow\log(k)</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Confidence is normalized inverse entropy </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\leftarrow 1-(H/H_{\max})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\leftarrow 1-(H/H_{\max})</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="algorithm2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.16" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.6.1 </span>Baseline prompts</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below we define the instruction that was provided to each baseline model:</p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:0.5cm;">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Base Model: <span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">‘‘Let’s think step by step and output the final answer within <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\backslash\backslash\text{{boxed}}\{\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>\</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">boxed</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\backslash\backslash\text{{boxed}}\{\}</annotation></semantics></math>’’</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">L1-Max: <span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">‘‘Let’s think step by step and output the final answer within <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\backslash\backslash\text{{boxed}}\{\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>\</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">boxed</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\backslash\backslash\text{{boxed}}\{\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Think for maximum 10000 tokens.’’</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">LC-R1: <span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">‘‘ Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\backslash\backslash\text{{boxed}}\{\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>\</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">boxed</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\backslash\backslash\text{{boxed}}\{\}</annotation></semantics></math>’’</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">AdaptThink: No prompt, just the question</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">TokenSkip: <span id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">‘‘&lt;|im_start|&gt;system You are a helpful assistant.&lt;|im_end|&gt; &lt;|im_start|&gt;user Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}. question&lt;|eot_id|&gt;0.5&lt;|eot_id|&gt;&lt;|im_end|&gt; &lt;|im_start|&gt;assistant’’</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Compute Used</h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All training was done on 4*A100 (80GB).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
